      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Using over-the-counter medications like ibuprofen and hydrocortisone can help alleviate pain and inflammation, but they're not a substitute for professional medical advice or treatment. It's crucial to get a proper assessment to avoid any potential complications. At minimum, optimizing self-care - with considerations such as keeping the area clean, avoiding tight clothing, and avoiding scratching - can be part of how you manage the symptoms until you're able to see a healthcare provider. Remember, however, that some health issues require later care, so it's very important to try and get seen as soon as possible. If you can't find an immediate way to see someone, it might be worth reaching out to a telemedicine service, which can provide you with some guidance over the phone. Some workplaces may even have a workers' compensation office that can assist in scheduling medical appointments. Your health should not be underestimated; taking precautions early could save time and ensure better care in the long run.",
      "source": "target",
